WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.554
- Good morning, believe nation
today's message is evolve.

00:00:04.554 --> 00:00:06.137
Over to you, Usher.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:10.783
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:10.783 --> 00:00:13.230
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:16.730
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:20.454
- Well, I mean, the thing
is we all have to set goals

00:00:20.454 --> 00:00:21.621
for ourselves.

00:00:22.872 --> 00:00:26.539
I mean, our plain
destination is to be busy.

00:00:28.244 --> 00:00:32.411
And to, you know, adjust to
whatever you're introduced to.

00:00:34.624 --> 00:00:37.054
And what I mean by that
is, okay as an entertainer

00:00:37.054 --> 00:00:39.939
I started off as a singer.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:42.415
You know, I grew to become
a dancer and a performer.

00:00:42.415 --> 00:00:44.569
After becoming a performer,
then I became an actor.

00:00:44.569 --> 00:00:46.754
After becoming an actor,
I became an entrepreneur,

00:00:46.754 --> 00:00:49.732
after becoming an entrepreneur
I become an entertainer

00:00:49.732 --> 00:00:53.110
on a different level of
introducing other artists.

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:56.132
Then after that I became a mentor.

00:00:56.132 --> 00:01:00.610
So I think just to continue
to evolve in a way that is

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:04.193
beneficial for growth
of myself and others.

00:01:06.157 --> 00:01:08.543
My likeness to continue to
be remembered throughout

00:01:08.543 --> 00:01:12.435
history and associated
with something great.

00:01:12.435 --> 00:01:13.268
- Wow.

00:01:15.259 --> 00:01:18.926
- For me, there's a
mantra that I do live by

00:01:21.589 --> 00:01:25.339
and it is that the
journey of the destination

00:01:27.249 --> 00:01:30.052
is really what it's all about.

00:01:30.052 --> 00:01:34.219
The pursuit is more important
than the actual destination.

00:01:37.965 --> 00:01:41.024
So as long as you are moving,
as long as you are working,

00:01:41.024 --> 00:01:42.627
that is the destination.

00:01:42.627 --> 00:01:44.051
- Wow.

00:01:44.051 --> 00:01:45.047
- The journey.

00:01:45.047 --> 00:01:47.555
Really it is simply that, the
journey is the destination.

00:01:47.555 --> 00:01:48.481
- I agree.

00:01:48.481 --> 00:01:50.736
- As long as you're working, you're good.

00:01:50.736 --> 00:01:52.585
- This is, I think, one of
the most important lessons

00:01:52.585 --> 00:01:55.387
for entrepreneurs to learn
because the way that you think

00:01:55.387 --> 00:01:58.303
something is going to
work out is rarely the way

00:01:58.303 --> 00:01:59.168
that it actually works out.

00:01:59.168 --> 00:02:01.087
And once you get into it
and you start experimenting

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:03.443
and start testing and start
talking to people and as you

00:02:03.443 --> 00:02:06.349
change and grow as a human
being, your business needs to

00:02:06.349 --> 00:02:08.290
change alongside of you.

00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:11.460
One of the most important
things I think is crucial

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.979
to understand is, as an entrepreneur,

00:02:13.979 --> 00:02:18.356
you need to be insanely
stubborn and flexible.

00:02:18.356 --> 00:02:21.321
You're stubborn around the
why, you're stubborn around

00:02:21.321 --> 00:02:24.321
the mission, you're stubborn
around your one word,

00:02:24.321 --> 00:02:26.637
you're stubborn around your
values, you're stubborn

00:02:26.637 --> 00:02:29.694
around the things that
really really matter.

00:02:29.694 --> 00:02:33.594
You're stubborn around the
why, but you're flexible around

00:02:33.594 --> 00:02:36.154
the what and the how.

00:02:36.154 --> 00:02:38.868
Because that's going to
change a million times as you

00:02:38.868 --> 00:02:40.096
build it up.

00:02:40.096 --> 00:02:43.094
And so if I look at my
career and what I've done,

00:02:43.094 --> 00:02:44.401
what's the why?

00:02:44.401 --> 00:02:48.296
The real why for me is
because in my first business

00:02:48.296 --> 00:02:49.686
I struggled a lot.

00:02:49.686 --> 00:02:51.818
I struggled as an
entrepreneur, I was making $300

00:02:51.818 --> 00:02:55.639
a month, I felt like
garbage, I felt like I had no

00:02:55.639 --> 00:02:57.091
value to give.

00:02:57.091 --> 00:02:59.956
I had the lowest self-confidence
than any point in my life

00:02:59.956 --> 00:03:02.323
when I had that first
business as an entrepreneur.

00:03:02.323 --> 00:03:05.289
And when I found my way
through and we had some success

00:03:05.289 --> 00:03:08.764
and I sold the business I
wanted to make it easier

00:03:08.764 --> 00:03:11.649
for entrepreneurs to get through.

00:03:11.649 --> 00:03:13.955
I didn't want other people
to struggle as much as

00:03:13.955 --> 00:03:15.948
I had to struggle.

00:03:15.948 --> 00:03:17.837
That's the why and it's still the why now.

00:03:17.837 --> 00:03:21.675
That was when I was 22
and how old am I now?

00:03:21.675 --> 00:03:22.508
Almost 37.

00:03:23.484 --> 00:03:27.883
15 years of the same why,
the same driving force,

00:03:27.883 --> 00:03:29.642
to help entrepreneurs.

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:32.483
The how, the what has changed.

00:03:32.483 --> 00:03:34.823
It started off with me being
a speaker and I got invited

00:03:34.823 --> 00:03:38.121
to speak at a bunch of different
events around the world

00:03:38.121 --> 00:03:39.333
and it was great.

00:03:39.333 --> 00:03:40.744
And I still do some.

00:03:40.744 --> 00:03:43.769
It transitioned to me doing
a website and having the

00:03:43.769 --> 00:03:47.672
most popular website with
famous entrepreneur stories

00:03:47.672 --> 00:03:49.248
online.

00:03:49.248 --> 00:03:51.715
It transitioned to me
starting a YouTube channel and

00:03:51.715 --> 00:03:53.331
making these videos for you guys,

00:03:53.331 --> 00:03:56.469
it transitioned to me
writing a book with a major

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:59.700
publishing house, Penguin (mumbles) house.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:02.544
In my head I'm thinking
about having an entrepreneur

00:04:02.544 --> 00:04:04.251
cafe, a place for
entrepreneurs to come together

00:04:04.251 --> 00:04:07.107
and work on their business
instead of just having

00:04:07.107 --> 00:04:10.367
to go to a regular coffee
shop that's designed for

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:13.638
entrepreneurs and there's
the videos up on the screen

00:04:13.638 --> 00:04:16.311
that motivate them and
there's simple business plans

00:04:16.311 --> 00:04:18.525
to look through and there's
paintings and quotes that

00:04:18.525 --> 00:04:19.672
all are related to helping entrepreneurs.

00:04:19.672 --> 00:04:22.000
I see this vision in my head
of having an entrepreneur

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.056
coffee shop.

00:04:23.056 --> 00:04:25.259
And some point we'll probably
get into the Evan Carmichael

00:04:25.259 --> 00:04:29.426
virtual reality put on
your goggles and experience

00:04:31.089 --> 00:04:32.248
entrepreneurship.

00:04:32.248 --> 00:04:34.718
You know, it's going to change.

00:04:34.718 --> 00:04:37.247
And it's great and you need
change as an entrepreneur.

00:04:37.247 --> 00:04:38.709
If you're doing the same
thing over and over again

00:04:38.709 --> 00:04:40.132
you're gong to get bored.

00:04:40.132 --> 00:04:44.874
And too many entrepreneurs
get stuck on one specific

00:04:44.874 --> 00:04:47.707
execution of the how and the what.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:52.636
And you're locked into one
product, locked into one service

00:04:52.636 --> 00:04:55.686
and then maybe that even has some success.

00:04:55.686 --> 00:04:57.522
Maybe that starts making you some money,

00:04:57.522 --> 00:04:59.413
maybe that starts giving
you some impact and some

00:04:59.413 --> 00:05:00.481
real benefit.

00:05:00.481 --> 00:05:03.517
And then it prevents you
from going out and evolving.

00:05:03.517 --> 00:05:06.518
I can't tell you how many
entrepreneurs I've run into

00:05:06.518 --> 00:05:08.759
that are bored of their business
and they want to move on.

00:05:08.759 --> 00:05:10.518
How are you bored of your business?

00:05:10.518 --> 00:05:14.387
They're bored of their
business because they got stuck

00:05:14.387 --> 00:05:17.892
on keeping the same how and what.

00:05:17.892 --> 00:05:20.555
And losing sight of the why.

00:05:20.555 --> 00:05:23.679
Why is always most important,
be stubborn around the why

00:05:23.679 --> 00:05:26.179
and you'll continue to evolve.

00:05:27.106 --> 00:05:30.618
And have the courage to
introduce new products,

00:05:30.618 --> 00:05:32.693
introduce new services, go
in a completely different

00:05:32.693 --> 00:05:36.939
direction as long as it's
aligned with your why.

00:05:36.939 --> 00:05:39.235
So the question of the day
is I'm curious what your

00:05:39.235 --> 00:05:42.416
why is in your business
and what your current what

00:05:42.416 --> 00:05:43.916
or how is as well.

00:05:44.936 --> 00:05:47.171
Leave it in the comments
below, I'm going to join in the

00:05:47.171 --> 00:05:48.094
discussion.

00:05:48.094 --> 00:05:50.247
I also want to give a quick
shoutout to Peter Arca.

00:05:50.247 --> 00:05:52.433
Peter, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:05:52.433 --> 00:05:55.805
Your One Word, it really
means a lot to me and I hope

00:05:55.805 --> 00:05:57.858
you're enjoying the read.

00:05:57.858 --> 00:06:00.641
So thank you guys again for
watching, I believe in you,

00:06:00.641 --> 00:06:03.242
I hope you continue to believe
in yourself and whatever

00:06:03.242 --> 00:06:05.009
your one word is.

00:06:05.009 --> 00:06:07.305
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:06:07.305 --> 00:06:09.711
for another shot of Entspresso.

